00:17:24.260 --> 00:17:29.080
"Blue phosphor. Out of the common phosphors, blue phosphor is of moderate levels of energy. It can exist in both organic and mineral forms."

00:17:29.080 --> 00:17:31.520
*audio gets progressively faster* "The mineral form is most commonly found in the metallic sand of the Barrens."

00:17:31.520 --> 00:17:34.460
"The organic form is most commonly found in phosphor shrimp and their secretions."

00:17:34.460 --> 00:17:39.840
"Although the light emissions of the blue phosphor is powerful, it has what I would describe as a "self-conserving" properties...that is to say, the glow may not be constant."

00:17:39.840 --> 00:17:42.620
"Most forms of the blue phosphor will stop glowing if left undisturbed for long periods of time."

00:17:42.620 --> 00:17:47.160
"If using blue phosphor to power machines, a motor should be set at a baseline level of activity to ensure constant agitation of the phosphor."

00:17:47.160 --> 00:17:48.860
"Alternatively, live phosphor shrimp can be used."

00:17:49.080 --> 00:17:51.440
"Green phosphor. Out of the three common phosphors, green phosphor is of the highest energy."

00:17:51.440 --> 00:17:53.660
"It is also the rarest of the common phosphors, as it can only be found in organic form."

00:17:53.660 --> 00:17:56.200
"Known sources include the sap of phosphor trees, fireflies, and various mosses."

00:17:56.200 --> 00:18:00.880
"Although this phosphor is present in the ubiquitous ground covering moss in the Glen, it is only in minute amounts and is almost impossible to concentrate."

00:18:00.880 --> 00:18:05.500
"Green phosphor is ideal for industrial use. However, due to its relative scarcity and past overharvesting, there is currently no reliable source."

00:18:05.500 --> 00:18:07.340
"Thankfully, at least locals of the Glen still have enough to get by."

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:09.980
"Red phosphor. Out of the common phosphors, red phosphor is of the lowest energy."

00:18:09.980 --> 00:18:12.120
"It exists exclusively in mineral form and can only give light when in solution."

00:18:12.120 --> 00:18:15.180
"The dilute red phosphor abundant in the city's water channels can be concentrated and induced with currents."

00:18:15.180 --> 00:18:17.140
This can create an official high-energy state with greater luminosity."

00:18:17.140 --> 00:18:19.840
"One major caveat is the phosphor in this supernaturated solution will precipitate out rather quickly."

00:18:19.840 --> 00:18:22.020
"As soon as the phosphor re-crystalizes, it loses its glow permanently."

00:18:22.020 --> 00:18:25.200
"If using supersaturated red phosphor as a power source, make sure there are proper facilities or services that can replace it frequently."

